cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or tool, please cite it as below."
title: "SWHForest: A Structure-Aware Catalog for Pointer-Only Code Corpora"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
# The license below covers the code (MIT). The license of the released data
# (data/release/) is stated in README.md, section "Licensing".
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Feature tables, a sharded structural index and view manifests for a 40% uniform
  hash-selected sample of ten Stack-Edu languages, keyed by Software Heritage
  identifiers and distributed without any source text, with the swhforest Python
  package that builds and queries them. The data license is given in README.md.
authors:
  - family-names: "Pennino"
    given-names: "Federico"
    affiliation: "University of Bologna"
repository-code: "https://github.com/halykoss/swhforest"
keywords:
  - code corpus
  - software heritage
  - abstract syntax tree
  - dataset curation
  - structural catalog
